 "stamp_convention": "16:00-NY stamp convention (frozen): TD serves date-only stamps (YYYY-MM-DD, no intraday component), one bar per date, strictly monotone. The cycle's frozen decision clock (\u00a74 F3) reads the bar dated D as the completed daily session whose decision close is 16:00 America/New_York on date D; state forms on completed bar t; entry at bar t+1 open, exit at bar t+1 close. The 16:00-NY assignment is the cycle's clock law, not a vendor claim; the vendor stamp is a calendar date.",
 "violation_law": "OHLC micro-rounding inconsistencies are COUNTED and disclosed, never repaired or ffilled (vintage law: the bytes stay exactly as served); non-positive prices, duplicate or non-date stamps abort fail-closed"
